From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Braumann <ripetitor@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:20:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: pm_domains: survive domain handshake failures
 during RM66 bring-up

Two issues observed on ELTAY RM66 over UART with the BSP 6.1 kernel:

1. The driver calls panic() unconditionally when a power domain does not
   reach the requested idle/on state within 10 ms. The first probe-time
   failure aborts the boot before init runs, and the dev_err naming the
   domain is lost because the FIQ console is not printing yet.
2. With the panic removed the boot advances, but a genpd power-off work
   has been observed stuck on the PMU mutex (RCU stall from
   genpd_power_off_work_fn, boot never reaches init).

Report handshake failures through the existing dev_err paths and make the
whole workaround opt-in: "always_on" stays off by default and the historic
panics are kept unless it is set, since this patch directory is shared with
every other vendor 6.1 board. ELTAY RM66 enables it per board with
pm_domains.always_on=1 in its extra kernel arguments, so power-off requests
are skipped and the domains stay powered until the root cause is identified
on a booting system.
This is a bring-up mitigation; revert once the failing domain is fixed.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Braumann <ripetitor@proton.me>
---
 drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
@@ -132,7 +132,15 @@
 };
 
 static struct rockchip_pmu *g_pmu;
-static bool pm_domain_always_on;
+/*
+ * RM66 bring-up: genpd power-off work has been observed stuck on the PMU
+ * mutex (RCU stall from genpd_power_off_work_fn), and the same handshakes
+ * abort early probes. Boards that hit this can skip power-off requests and
+ * the panics below by booting with pm_domains.always_on=1 (ELTAY RM66 does
+ * that from its board config); the default stays off because this patch
+ * directory is shared with other vendor 6.1 boards.
+ */
+static bool pm_domain_always_on;
 
 module_param_named(always_on, pm_domain_always_on, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(always_on,
@@ -633,7 +641,8 @@
 
 	return ret;
 error:
-	panic("panic_on_set_idle set ...\n");
+	if (!pm_domain_always_on)
+		panic("panic_on_set_idle set ...\n");
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -971,7 +980,8 @@
 	return ret;
 
 error:
-	panic("panic_on_set_domain set ...\n");
+	if (!pm_domain_always_on)
+		panic("panic_on_set_domain set ...\n");
 	return ret;
 }
 
